viation and so  going back to the example of the  Microsoft malware prediction here is the  visualization we have for the future  importances so the the colored bar is  the value of the mean so the mean is  around here and then the standard  deviation is the black wire around it  and if you scroll all the way down  you'll see that the OS version is  actually the most harmful future so you  shouldn't treat e8 include it in your  model yeah so that's it install it try  it out it's on github just some caveats  it is slow although we paralyze because  you iterate over all the features and  it's bound to happen it's so far still  misleading at like the permutation  importance when it comes to correlated  features but we're working on that and  we're going to implement a leave n  features out component which would then  flag all the correlated features and  give them the same importance if let's  say they're very very highly correlated  thank you and also we're hiring data  engineers and software engineers  [Applause]

